// Title: Potential Memory Dumping Activity Via LiveKD
// Sigma ID: a85f7765-698a-4088-afa0-ecfbf8d01fa4
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects execution of LiveKD based on PE metadata or image name
// False positives:
//   - Administration and debugging activity (must be investigated)
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/livekd
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_livekd_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\livekd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\livekd64.exe") or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "livekd.exe"
